"Note the `mut xs` parameter heads: vecs are handles, so an in-place swap "
"inside a call is shared with the bank — but **writing** through the handle "
"requires the `mut` binding head, while mere reads (and `push`) do not. That "
"asymmetry is the mut-binding law, and every algorithm in this file declares "
"it ([Modules and visibility](../reference/modules-and-visibility.md))."
