#: src/examples/03-plugin.md:56
msgid ""
"The moderator rules themselves are plain rut — flood control (three "
"consecutive messages from one sender mutes them), muted users rejected on "
"rejoin, a `!stats` command, tick heartbeats:"
msgstr ""

#: src/examples/03-plugin.md:60
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"pub fn on_msg(mut self, user: str, text: str) {\n"
"    if (self.is_muted(user)) {\n"
"        self.say(\"muted\", user);\n"
"    } else if (text == \"!stats\") {\n"
"        self.say(\"direct\", f\"{user}: {self.stats()}\");\n"
"    } else {\n"
"        if (user == self.last_sender) {\n"
"            self.streak += 1;\n"
"        } else {\n"
"            self.last_sender = user;\n"
"            self.streak = 1;\n"
"        }\n"
"        if (self.streak == 3) {\n"
"            self.muted.push(user);\n"
"            self.mutes += 1;\n"
"            self.say(\"system\", f\"{user} muted for flooding\");\n"
"        } else {\n"
"            self.msgs += 1;\n"
"            self.say(\"broadcast\", f\"<{user}> {text}\");\n"
"        }\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/examples/03-plugin.md:85
msgid ""
"Every bus write funnels through one private `say(topic, payload)` — the "
"business logic never spells a crossing."
msgstr ""

#: src/examples/03-plugin.md:88
msgid "The handshake: both opaque directions meet"
msgstr ""

#: src/examples/03-plugin.md:90
msgid ""
"Closures cannot cross the boundary in either direction, so callbacks "
"register **by name**: the plugin hands the host the export names it wants "
"wired to each topic, and returns the handle to its own state (`init` is the "
"entire handshake — bus box in, state handle out):"
msgstr ""

#: src/examples/03-plugin.md:95
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"entry fn init(bus: opaque) -> opaque {\n"
"    subscribe(bus, \"join\", \"on_join\");\n"
"    subscribe(bus, \"msg\", \"on_msg\");\n"
"    subscribe(bus, \"leave\", \"on_leave\");\n"
"    subscribe(bus, \"tick\", \"on_tick\");\n"
"    let mod_: ?Moderator = Moderator.new(bus);\n"
"    return opaque(mod_);\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/examples/03-plugin.md:106
msgid ""
"rut's moderator state comes back as a **rut-constructed** `opaque` — the "
"host holds the handle and passes it back on every event."
msgstr ""

#: src/examples/03-plugin.md:108
msgid ""
"the host's `EventBus` goes in as a **host-constructed** `Opaque<EventBus>` — "
"`subscribe` and `emit` are that box's callbacks, reached only through the "
"borrow guards ([Value boundary and borrows](../reference/value-boundary.md), "
"[Embedding and native modules](../reference/embedding.md))."
msgstr ""

#: src/examples/03-plugin.md:114
msgid "The re-entrant call: `emit` re-enters rut mid-op"
msgstr ""

#: src/examples/03-plugin.md:116
msgid ""
"The host binds the two `server` rows over its bus. The `emit` body is the "
"interesting one — while the emitting handler is still parked mid-op, it "
"makes a **nested** `vm.call(\"render_line\")` to format the wire line:"
msgstr ""

#: src/examples/03-plugin.md:122 src/reference/embedding.md:60
#: src/reference/host-fns.md:155
msgid "\"server\""
msgstr ""

#: src/examples/03-plugin.md:123 src/reference/embedding.md:61
#: src/reference/host-fns.md:158
msgid "\"emit\""
msgstr ""

#: src/examples/03-plugin.md:127
msgid "\"render_line\""
msgstr ""

#: src/examples/03-plugin.md:138
msgid ""
"(The comment above this code in the source is worth reading too.) The bus "
"stays mutably borrowed _across_ the nested call — the value boundary's "
"borrow guard is what makes that sound: a second `emit` fired from inside "
"`render_line` would trap on the guard instead of racing. On the rut side, "
"`render_line` is the one-line entry the host re-enters — pure string work, "
"so it runs on its own (the line it prints below is the transcript's "
"broadcast row):"
msgstr ""

#: src/examples/03-plugin.md:146
