msgstr ""

#: src/reference/primitive-types.md:34
msgid "Size and members"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/primitive-types.md:36
msgid ""
"`.len()` is the sequence member shared by every sequence: `[T]`, `Vec<T>`, "
"`str` (codepoints), `bytes` (octets). There is no `.length` property or "
"`.count()` variant anywhere in the language."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/primitive-types.md:40
msgid ""
"`str` members: `len()`, `code()`, `code_at(i)`, `encode() -> bytes`, "
"`slice(from, to) -> str`, `starts_with(from, head) -> bool`, `scan(from, "
"set) -> i64`. `bytes` members: `len()`, `decode() -> str` (UTF-8, lossy), "
"`clone() -> bytes`; type-methods `bytes.zeroed(n) -> bytes` and "
"`bytes.from(a: [u8]) -> bytes`. `str.encode()` and `bytes.decode()` convert "
"between text and octets."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/primitive-types.md:48
msgid "One regime: primitives by value, everything else shared"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/primitive-types.md:50
msgid ""
"Primitives (`u8..u64`, `i8..i64`, `f32`/`f64`, `bool`) and `fn` values copy "
"on assignment, passing, and return — plain slot moves. **Every other type is "
"a refcounted heap cell handle**: assignment shares, and mutation through any "
"alias is visible through all of them — struct and class instances, `str`, "
"`bytes`, `Vec`, `[T]`, enums, `opaque` boxes, trait-typed values, `?T` boxes "
"alike. Writing is gated by the `mut`\\-binding law (see [Modules and "
"visibility](modules-and-visibility.md)), never by the sharing."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/primitive-types.md:59
msgid ""
"There is no eager copy and no `own(x)`: **`bytes.clone()` is the one copy "
"escape hatch**. There is no `&`/`*` syntax anywhere. `==` on cells is "
"**identity** (the raw slot compare); `str`/`bytes` compare by content — the "
"full table is in [Rc, dispose, and identity](rc-dispose-identity.md)."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/primitive-types.md:65
msgid ""
"No `box<T>`, no loans: a loan needs an exclusivity proof, and rut has no "
"borrow checker. The construct is rejected, not deferred. The only borrows "
"anywhere are host-side, call-scoped ones at the embedding boundary."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/primitive-types.md:70
msgid "Tuples and the answer channel"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/primitive-types.md:72
msgid ""
"Tuples are first-class values: type `(A, B)`, value `(a, b)`, numeric field "
"access `.0`, `.1`, .., destructuring:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/primitive-types.md:80
msgid ""
"**`(?T, err)` — concretely `(value, ok)` / `(T, str)` — is the answer "
"channel** for results and errors. The convention is law:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/primitive-types.md:83
msgid "empty err + a value = **success**"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/primitive-types.md:84
msgid "empty err + `nil` = **\"not found\"** (a legitimately absent value)"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/primitive-types.md:85
msgid "non-empty err = **failed**"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/primitive-types.md:87
msgid ""
"`checked_add`/`checked_sub`/`checked_mul` return `(value, ok)` — `false` "
"exactly on overflow, `value` the wrapped bits either way."
msgstr ""

