#: src/reference/value-boundary.md:3
msgid ""
"The one place tagged values exist: the host boundary. Inside the VM, "
"registers are untagged slots ([the VM heap](vm-heap.md)); crossing into Rust "
"materializes a checked, borrow-guarded value. The currency of the boundary "
"is **typed Rust**: the registered closure's parameter types and the "
"`vm.call` return type are the whole contract. The crate-internal marshaling "
"formats (`Value`, `Slot`) never leave the VM crate."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/value-boundary.md:12
msgid ""
"What may cross is a **compile-time property of the surface**. A violation is "
"a compile error on the declaration or binding — never a call-time failure."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/value-boundary.md:15
msgid ""
"**Parameters** cross over: the primitives (`i8`–`i64`, `u8`–`u64`, `f32`, "
"`f64`, `bool`), `str`, `bytes`, and `opaque`."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/value-boundary.md:17
msgid ""
"**Returns** cross over the same set **plus** the answer optionals `?str`, "
"`?bytes`, `?opaque`."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/value-boundary.md:19
msgid "Tuples cross field-by-field; each field must itself cross."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/value-boundary.md:20
msgid ""
"Entry fns follow the same rule in both directions: `?T` crosses iff `T` "
"crosses, decoded nil-flattened."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/value-boundary.md:22
msgid ""
"Everything else — dataclasses, classes, `Vec<T>`, `[T]`, trait-typed values, "
"closures — stays inside the VM. Seal polymorphic values in the erasure box: "
"`opaque(v)` at the call, `opaque.downcast<T>(v)` after ([opaque — erasure "
"and downcast](opaque.md))."
msgstr ""

