#: src/reference/reflection.md:3
msgid ""
"Reflection is a **trait**, not a keyword privilege. `Reflectable` is the "
"mechanism protocol; compiler auto-implementations (dataclasses, enums) and "
"builtin-impl registry entries (enums, records, `Vec`, `[T]`) fill it for the "
"data world; classes opt in by hand with a **curated** view. Libraries layer "
"contracts on top and take trait-object-typed consumers or bounded producers. "
"Nothing in the language names a builtin; no strings are matched; nothing "
"changes under `--release` stripping. Userland serde is the proving "
"application."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reflection.md:12
msgid ""
"Status: this page specifies the reflection surface; the protocols are not "
"yet wired into the engine. The surfaces it builds on — traits, "
"[opaque](opaque.md), reified descriptors ([reified types](reified-types.md)) "
"— are live."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reflection.md:17
msgid "The protocols"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reflection.md:19
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"// reflect/reflect.d.rut\n"
"pub trait Reflectable {                     // the mechanism protocol\n"
"    fn reflect(self) -> opaque;             // exact descriptor handle\n"
"    fn arity(self) -> i32;                  // children of THIS value\n"
"    fn child(self, i: i32) -> ?opaque;      // i-th child, boxed\n"
"}\n"
"pub trait Deserializable requires Reflectable { }\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

