#: src/reference/bundles.md:292
msgid "The std tree on a CDN — the per-package delivery"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/bundles.md:294
msgid ""
"The std tree (`rut/`) ships as **committed** per-package bundles at "
"`dist/std/<pkg>.rutbundle` — one bundle per package a `[deps]` row can spell "
"(15 today). jsDelivr's gh lane serves repo files at a ref, so the artifacts "
"ARE the delivery and the publish act is a git tag:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/bundles.md:299
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[deps]\n"
"http = { url = "
"\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/hpp2334/rut@<tag>/dist/std/http.rutbundle\",\n"
"        sha256 = \"<64-hex>\" }\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/bundles.md:305
msgid ""
"`<tag>`/`<sha256>` are placeholders — real pins live in the examples "
"(anti-rot: docs never rot pins). The laws:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/bundles.md:308
msgid ""
"**Committed artifacts, immutable tags.** `scripts/pack-std.cjs` packs all 15 "
"(deterministic — same input ⇒ byte-identical, so freshness is a pure "
"equality gate: `--check` repacks and byte-compiles, no network); `--pins` "
"rewrites the example manifests' url/sha256 rows; `--tag` prints the publish "
"commands. Tags advance (`std-vNN`) and are never re-pointed — jsDelivr "
"caches aggressively."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/bundles.md:314
msgid ""
"**What a compiled bundle serves.** Instantiation is owner-anchored: a "
"compiled owner carries the generic instantiations its own pack closure "
"spelled in its ledger — and, the generic-source riding law, a compiled pkg "
"whose surface exports generics also rides the source that serves "
"consumer-spelled shapes: at the consumer's link a request the ledger lacks "
"lowers the ridden text in the consumer's session and compiles the "
"monomorphized body under the declaring pkg's spec (one row program-wide, "
"nothing persisted). So the CDN lane delivers **host surfaces** (v6 decl "
"bundles), **concrete-class libs** (`http`, `ink`, `strbuild` — methods cross "
"on the surface's inherent rows), **and the generic owners** (`pouch`, "
"`nmapset`, `json`, `async_host` — `Vec<Todo>`, `Map<K,V>`, `decodeJson<T>` "
"compile at the link from the ridden source). A bundle that predates the "
"riding refuses a consumer-spelled shape loudly and says so (re-pack it), and "
"a bundle-mounted json names its pack-time dev closure in its ledger, so the "
"consumer's closure must contain those names (`pouch`, `nmapset` beside "
"`json` — the six-pin law)."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/bundles.md:331
msgid ""
"**Duplicate mounts are safe.** Two archives may carry the same group "
"(`json`'s and `http`'s closures both carry `strbuild`): first-mount-wins "
"mounts one body, and the per-archive ledger namespacing keeps every binary's "
"ids resolving through its own archive's rows. Pin sets stay minimal-top "
"anyway — a closed bundle carries the rest."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/bundles.md:338
msgid "Loading"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/bundles.md:340
msgid ""
"A bundle is one more resolution source alongside the directory form — same "
"name resolution, same compile, same splice rules:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/bundles.md:344
msgid "// from a file\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/bundles.md:345
msgid "\"vendor/plugin.rutbundle\""
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/bundles.md:345
msgid "// from bytes (embedders, tests, wasm)\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/bundles.md:347
msgid "\"mem\""
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/bundles.md:350
msgid ""
"After mounting, the package name resolves exactly as the directory form does "
"— with one difference: a compiled group's body is the decoded program "
"itself. The graph assigns it a fresh scope, rebases its packed ids through "
"the ledger, and pushes it; source groups mount as sources and compile (or "
"splice) exactly as a directory world. Then the normal pipeline takes over "
"([Loading and the embed loop](loading.md)). Loose directories and loose "
"`.rut` files stay valid share layouts; the bundle packages them, nothing "
"requires it."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/bundles.md:362
msgid "# default output: a sibling of the dir\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/bundles.md:366
msgid ""
"The packed form and its directory compile to identical programs — pinned by "
"tests (the linked binaries are equal)."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:3
msgid ""
"One directory is one module; its `rut.toml` names the exact package it "
"answers to and how to reach its surface and body. The manifest is what makes "
"the directory **the runnable unit**: `rut run <dir>` (or its packed "
"`.rutbundle`) is the only run lane — a loose `.rut` file is not a program "
"([the rut CLI](cli.md)). This page is the manifest grammar, the resolution "
"laws, and where everything lives in the toolchain tree."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:11
msgid "The manifest"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:13
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"# rut/pouch/rut.toml — a body package\n"
"name = \"pouch\"\n"
"entry.lib = \"./pouch.rut\"\n"
"\n"
"# rut/calc/rut.toml — a pure declaration surface (a host pkg)\n"
"name = \"calc\"\n"
"type = \"host\"\n"
"entry.type = \"./calc.d.rut\"\n"
"\n"
"# a consumer (an app directory)\n"
"name = \"app\"\n"
"entry.lib = \"./app.rut\"\n"
"\n"
"[deps]\n"
"pouch = { path = \"../pouch\" }\n"
"ink   = { path = \"../ink\" }\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:32
msgid "The keys, all of them:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:34
msgid "key"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:36
msgid "`name`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:36
msgid ""
"the package's use-path name: bare `[a-zA-Z0-9_]+` only. A scoped or quoted "
"spelling is a manifest error."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:37
msgid "`entry.lib`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:37
msgid "the body: one `.rut` file (or `.rutc`\\-style artifacts where supported)"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:38
msgid "`entry.libs`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:38
msgid "ordered extra `.rut` files — the **multi-lib entry** (below)"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:39
msgid ""
"the declared kind: `type = \"host\"` for a **host pkg** — a pure declaration "
"surface whose `host fn`s the embedder binds at load ([Host fns and "
"declaration files](host-fns.md)); `type = \"lib\"` (or absent) is the "
"ordinary source package. The kind is never inferred — an `entry.type`\\-only "
"manifest with no kind is an error naming both fixes"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:40
msgid "`entry.type`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:40
msgid ""
"the declaration surface: one `.d.rut` file. On a lib pkg it is documentation "
"surface (a surface-only dev state mounts as a declaration unit; `host fn` "
"text there is refused)"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:41 src/reference/dependency-kinds.md:139
msgid "`[deps]`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:41
msgid ""
"the transitively mounted dependencies — one source per descriptor: `pkg = { "
"path = \"...\" }` (relative to this manifest) or `pkg = { url = "
"\"https://…\", sha256 = \"<64-hex>\" }` (a remote `.rutbundle`, the pin "
"optional but recommended) ([Dependency kinds](dependency-kinds.md)). "
"`optional` is rejected here."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:42
msgid "`[peer-deps]`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:42
msgid ""
"presence-gated peers — descriptors accept `path`, `optional`, `lib` "
"([Dependency kinds](dependency-kinds.md))"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:43 src/reference/dependency-kinds.md:142
msgid "`[dev-deps]`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:43
msgid "mounted only while building/testing this pkg itself"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:44
msgid "`inline`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:44
msgid ""
"`true` forces source-inlining into every consumer instead of linking "
"(packages whose class methods must resolve at the call site — inherent impls "
"cross no surface yet; generic exports link on their own, their "
"instantiations owned by the declaring package)"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:45
msgid "`format`, `format_version`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:45
msgid ""
"bundle keys — ignored by directory loading, required by `rut pack` ([Module "
"bundles](bundles.md))"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:46
msgid "`[style]`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:46
msgid ""
"formatter knobs: `indent_width` (1–8, default 4), `max_width` (≥ 20, default "
"100). Schema-free at the manifest layer — unknown keys ride; malformed "
"values are formatter errors, never compile errors. Resolution: the nearest "
"ancestor manifest of the formatted file; no manifest → defaults."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:48
msgid ""
"The parser accepts only the TOML subset the format uses (comments, `key = "
"\"string\"`, dotted keys, `[section]`, inline tables), so the driver stays "
"dependency-free and wasm-compatible. Descriptors are key/value maps; unknown "
"descriptor keys are line-targeted manifest errors."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:54
msgid "Resolution laws"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:56
msgid ""
"**Exact, single-step.** A use path resolves only if a module with that "
"`name` is mounted. Nothing is derived from directories or file layouts."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:59
msgid ""
"**The walk is recursive, with a cycle guard; first mount wins.** An "
"already-mounted name (the embedder's, the root's, or an earlier dep's) is "
"never overwritten — which is what makes peer presence-by-name sound: the "
"consumer's own path for a package always beats the declarer's `path`."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:64
msgid ""
"**Name mismatch is an error.** A dep whose manifest `name` disagrees with "
"its key fails, naming both."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:66
msgid ""
"**The cross-table law.** A name in `[deps]` beside `[peer-deps]` or "
"`[dev-deps]` is an error naming both rows; peer + dev together is the "
"sanctioned pairing."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:69
msgid ""
"**`core` needs no `[deps]`** — the driver mounts it unconditionally; every "
"name still requires `use core::{ .. };` per [core and the swappable "
"packages](stdlib.md)."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:73
msgid "The multi-lib entry"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:75
msgid "A package's body may be split across files:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:77
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"name = \"ui\"\n"
"entry.lib  = \"./ui.rut\"\n"
"entry.libs = [\"./store.rut\", \"./t1.rut\"]\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:83
msgid ""
"The loader splices base-first, then `libs` in listed order, newline-joined, "
"into **one module** — one namespace, one visibility scope. A name private to "
"one file is visible to every other file of the package. The manifest is the "
"canonical order (the splice never reads a directory listing — same manifest "
"⇒ same module). A `libs` row without `lib`, a `.d.rut` element, or a file "
"named twice is a loud manifest error. This is assembly, not a language "
"include form — use paths stay inter-module."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:91
msgid ""
"Contrast with peer groups: group files are _presence-gated_ and therefore "
"impl-only; multi-lib files are unconditional and full module citizens — "
"types, functions, and `pub` surface are legal in any file."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:95
msgid "The toolchain tree"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:123
msgid ""
"Dependency line: `rut-lexer ← rut-ast ← rut-parser ← rut-driver → rut-lir → "
"rut-core ← rut-vm` (with `rut-vm-threaded` behind it; the driver sits on the "
"vm's `HostPkgContext`/`HostRegistry` for the installer lane), hosts "
"(`rut-std`, `rut-wasm`) on top, and `rut-cli`/`demo` above those. `rut-lsp` "
"sits on the frontend crates only — tokens, diagnostics, and symbols need no "
"VM."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:131
